From 4808848626ea90274125cd075ae942def2da3044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artemonim <Artemonim@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:43:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/23] =?UTF-8?q?feat(openrouter):=20service=20tiers=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20flex/priority=20and=20per-model=20overrides?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Focused split of #100711 (service-tier half), adapted to main's #104159
chokepoint shape: per-model agent.service_tier_overrides resolve at request
time in effective_request_overrides via _canonical_model_variants — no
per-surface plumbing; /model switches, fallback, cron and delegated children
pick their own model's tier.

- agent.service_tier accepts flex; OpenRouter routes carry flex/priority
  for any catalog model; first-party fast-mode behavior unchanged
- Precedence: session /fast pin > per-model override > global; the pin
  survives /model and clears on session reset (/fast normal pins normal)
- /fast status reports the effective tier (fast/flex/normal/auto/cold) for
  the session-effective model without the capability gate on CLI, gateway
  and TUI; switching to fast stays route-gated (now incl. OpenRouter)
- Auxiliary tasks gain a route-gated service_tier shortcut
- gateway.fast locale strings (all 17 catalogs), docs, cli-config example

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
